    "description": "MIM is the stablecoin minted by Abracadabra’s lending markets, where users borrow against interest-bearing crypto collateral (e.g., yield vault shares, LP tokens). Peg stability depends on overcollateralization and liquidation risk management across many collateral types, which can create complex cross-protocol contagion risk. Key risks include collateral depegs, liquidation cascades, oracle risk, and smart-contract risk across the integrated DeFi stack.",
